  "crewNotes": "Warm salty liquids are what work late — cup-o-noodles, broth, quesadillas. Dry food gets hard to swallow. Proven foods: PB&J, Uncrustables, Oreos, Nutter Butters, watermelon, pretzels.\n\nIf I'm struggling — tight stomach, hoarse voice, heart rate climbing, not eating — it's almost always SODIUM AND FLUID, not calories. Push an LMNT, not a gel. This is my known failure mode.\n\nWhen it's hot: refill my ice bandana and pour two cups of cold water over my head. Makes a massive difference. Offer it in case I forget to ask.\n\nSalt pills come in counted containers with the number in sharpie. Pills left = pills not taken. Check them at every stop and tell me the number.\n\nExpect two or more bathroom stops over the race. Normal for me. Not a problem. If I go and it's not solid, give me Imodium.\n\nWhen I go quiet, ask me direct questions with numbers: how many gels this leg, when did you last pee, what sounds good right now. Don't ask \"how are you feeling.\"\n\nI can nap 15–20 minutes and come back fine. Offer it if I'm fading.\n\nMusic only when I'm struggling - it's a tool, not background.\n\nI DNF'd here at mile 86 in 2025. The second night is the fight.",
